## 5. Import steps (optional - via the `overcut-api` skill)

1. Commit `skills/` into a repo connected to the target project -> `browseSkillsInRepo` to confirm discovery, then `createSkill` / `createSkills` (`repositoryId`, `slug` = folder name, `path`, `ref`, `name`, `description`).
2. `createAgent` for each `agents/*.agent.json` (with real `modelKey`, `skillIds`, `mcpServerIds`), then `setAgentSecrets` for its secrets.
3. `importWorkflow(file, name, projectId, agentMapping)` for each `workflows/*.workflow.json`, mapping every `refs.agents[].id` placeholder to the created agent id. This edits the **draft** - review in the UI, then `commitWorkflow` to go live.

Do not create secret values, `commitWorkflow`, or trigger runs without explicit confirmation.
